                </div>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;line-height:normal'>
                    <span style='color:black'>
                        * The rate includes Rs. 2200/- per sq. meter which is on
                        account of additional compensation payable to the farmers arising out of c
                        ourt’sorder.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify'>
                    <span style='color:black'>
                        Location charges
                        as stated below shall be payable in addition to the above rates of allotment.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;
  margin-bottom:6.0pt;margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;
  line-height:normal'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>
                            (i)<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
                            </span>
                        </span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        2.5% of current rate if plot is
                        facing 18 mtr. but less than 30 mtr. wide road.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;
  margin-bottom:6.0pt;margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;
  line-height:normal'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>
                            (ii)<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>
                                &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
                            </span>
                        </span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        5% of current rate if plot is
                        facing 30 mtr. or above wide road.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;
  margin-bottom:6.0pt;margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;
  line-height:normal'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>
                            (iii)<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>
                                &nbsp;
                            </span>
                        </span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        2.5% of current rate if plot is
                        facing /abutting green belt or park
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoListParagraphCxSpLast style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;
  margin-bottom:6.0pt;margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.25in;
  line-height:normal'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>
                            (iv)<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>
                                &nbsp;
                            </span>
                        </span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        2.5% of current rate if plot is a
                        corner plot.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:1.0in;text-align:justify;text-indent:-.5in'>
                    <span style='color:black'>
                        The maximum location charges would not exceed 10% of the
                        total premium of the plot.
                    </span>
                </p>
                <p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
  margin-left:.5in;text-align:justify'>
                    <b>
                        <span style='color:black'>
                            The rates
                            for IT/ITES projects are Rs. 16040/- per sq.mtrs. plus location benefit
                            charges as applicable and for these projects the terms &amp; conditions for
                            the institutional areas (IT/ITES) shall be applicable.
                        </span>
                    </b><span style='color:black'>
                        In these industrial units change of project will not be
                        permitted under any circumstances. The rate includes Rs. 2200/- per sq. meter
                        which is on account of additional compensation payable to the farmers arising
                        out of c ourt’s order.
                    </span>
                </p>
